skill: Quantitative Aptitude

@ Percentages | B
What is 25% of 480?
= 120
- 100
- 125
- 140
? 25% is one quarter, and 480 / 4 = 120.

@ Percentages | B
A value increases from 80 to 100. What is the percentage increase?
= 25%
- 20%
- 80%
- 125%
? Increase = 20, and 20 / 80 = 25%.

@ Percentages | I
A student scores 360 marks out of 600. What is the percentage?
= 60%
- 36%
- 55%
- 65%
? 360 / 600 x 100 = 60%.

@ Percentages | I
A price is increased by 10% and then decreased by 10%. What is the net change?
= 1% decrease
- No change
- 1% increase
- 10% decrease
? 1.10 x 0.90 = 0.99, which is a 1% decrease.

@ Percentages | A
Salary A is 25% more than salary B. By what percentage is B less than A?
= 20%
- 25%
- 15%
- 30%
? Let B = 100, then A = 125. The difference 25 is 20% of 125.

@ Percentages | I
40% of a number is 120. What is the number?
= 300
- 48
- 480
- 200
? If 40% = 120 then 100% = 120 / 0.4 = 300.

@ Profit and Loss | B
An item is bought for 200 and sold for 250. What is the profit percentage?
= 25%
- 20%
- 50%
- 30%
? Profit = 50 and 50 / 200 = 25%.

@ Profit and Loss | B
A bat bought for 500 is sold for 450. What is the loss percentage?
= 10%
- 5%
- 11%
- 15%
? Loss = 50 and 50 / 500 = 10%.

@ Profit and Loss | I
An article is sold for 540 at a loss of 10%. What is its cost price?
= 600
- 594
- 486
- 560
? SP = 0.9 x CP, so CP = 540 / 0.9 = 600.

@ Profit and Loss | I
A shopkeeper marks goods 20% above cost price and allows a 10% discount. What is the profit percentage?
= 8%
- 10%
- 12%
- 30%
? Selling price = 1.2 x 0.9 = 1.08 times the cost, so the profit is 8%.

@ Profit and Loss | I
The cost price of 12 articles equals the selling price of 10 articles. What is the profit percentage?
= 20%
- 10%
- 12%
- 25%
? Let each article cost 1, then 10 x SP = 12, so SP = 1.2 and the profit is 20%.

@ Profit and Loss | A
Two articles are sold at 1200 each. One gives a 20% profit and the other a 20% loss. What is the overall result?
= 4% loss
- No profit or loss
- 4% profit
- 2% loss
? Cost prices are 1000 and 1500, total 2500. Total sale is 2400, so the loss is 100 / 2500 = 4%.

@ Ratio and Proportion | B
Divide 120 in the ratio 3:5. What is the larger part?
= 75
- 45
- 60
- 80
? Total parts = 8, one part = 15, so the larger part is 5 x 15 = 75.

@ Ratio and Proportion | I
If 3 : x = 9 : 15, what is x?
= 5
- 3
- 9
- 45
? 3 / x = 9 / 15, so x = 3 x 15 / 9 = 5.

@ Ratio and Proportion | I
A : B = 2 : 3 and B : C = 4 : 5. What is A : B : C?
= 8 : 12 : 15
- 2 : 3 : 5
- 8 : 12 : 20
- 6 : 9 : 15
? Make B equal in both ratios: A:B = 8:12 and B:C = 12:15, so A:B:C = 8:12:15.

@ Ratio and Proportion | A
A 16 litre mixture contains milk and water in the ratio 5 : 3. How much water must be added to make the ratio 5 : 4?
= 2 litres
- 1 litre
- 3 litres
- 4 litres
? Milk = 10 L and water = 6 L. For 10 : x = 5 : 4, x = 8 L, so add 2 L.

@ Time and Work | B
A can complete a job in 10 days. What fraction of the job does A complete in one day?
= 1/10
- 10
- 1/5
- 1/100
? Work done per day is 1 divided by the number of days.

@ Time and Work | I
A can finish a job in 12 days and B in 6 days. How many days will they take working together?
= 4
- 9
- 6
- 3
? Combined rate = 1/12 + 1/6 = 3/12 = 1/4 per day, so 4 days.

@ Time and Work | I
A and B together finish a job in 8 days. A alone takes 12 days. How many days does B take alone?
= 24
- 20
- 4
- 18
? B's rate = 1/8 - 1/12 = 1/24, so B takes 24 days.

@ Time and Work | A
10 men complete a job in 15 days. How many days will 25 men take?
= 6
- 9
- 10
- 37.5
? Total work = 150 man-days. 150 / 25 = 6 days.

@ Time and Work | A
A tap fills a tank in 6 hours and a leak empties it in 12 hours. With both open, how long does the tank take to fill?
= 12 hours
- 4 hours
- 6 hours
- 18 hours
? Net rate = 1/6 - 1/12 = 1/12 per hour.

@ Time, Speed and Distance | B
A car travels at 60 km/h for 2.5 hours. What distance does it cover?
= 150 km
- 120 km
- 130 km
- 180 km
? Distance = speed x time = 60 x 2.5 = 150 km.

@ Time, Speed and Distance | I
Convert 72 km/h into metres per second.
= 20 m/s
- 18 m/s
- 25 m/s
- 72 m/s
? Multiply by 5/18: 72 x 5 / 18 = 20 m/s.

@ Time, Speed and Distance | I
A 150 m long train runs at 54 km/h. How long does it take to cross a pole?
= 10 seconds
- 15 seconds
- 9 seconds
- 27 seconds
? 54 km/h = 15 m/s, and 150 / 15 = 10 seconds.

@ Time, Speed and Distance | I
A person travels a distance at 60 km/h and returns at 40 km/h. What is the average speed for the whole trip?
= 48 km/h
- 50 km/h
- 52 km/h
- 45 km/h
? Average speed = 2 x 60 x 40 / (60 + 40) = 48 km/h.

@ Time, Speed and Distance | A
Two trains 100 m and 120 m long run in opposite directions at 36 km/h and 54 km/h. How long do they take to cross each other?
= 8.8 seconds
- 10 seconds
- 12.2 seconds
- 9.6 seconds
? Relative speed = 90 km/h = 25 m/s. Distance = 220 m, so time = 220 / 25 = 8.8 s.

@ Time, Speed and Distance | A
A boat has a speed of 12 km/h in still water and the stream flows at 3 km/h. How long does it take to go 45 km downstream?
= 3 hours
- 5 hours
- 3.75 hours
- 4 hours
? Downstream speed = 12 + 3 = 15 km/h, so time = 45 / 15 = 3 hours.

@ Simple and Compound Interest | B
What is the simple interest on 1000 at 10% per annum for 2 years?
= 200
- 100
- 210
- 220
? SI = P x R x T / 100 = 1000 x 10 x 2 / 100 = 200.

@ Simple and Compound Interest | I
What is the compound interest on 2000 at 10% per annum for 2 years, compounded annually?
= 420
- 400
- 440
- 410
? Amount = 2000 x 1.1 x 1.1 = 2420, so CI = 420.

@ Simple and Compound Interest | I
At simple interest a sum becomes 1.5 times itself in 5 years. What is the rate per annum?
= 10%
- 5%
- 12%
- 15%
? Interest is 50% of the principal over 5 years, so the rate is 10% per year.

@ Simple and Compound Interest | A
What is the difference between compound interest and simple interest on 5000 at 10% per annum for 2 years?
= 50
- 100
- 25
- 500
? For two years the difference is P x (R/100)^2 = 5000 x 0.01 = 50.

@ Simple and Compound Interest | I
At what annual rate of compound interest does 4000 become 4840 in 2 years?
= 10%
- 8%
- 12%
- 21%
? 4840 / 4000 = 1.21 = (1.10)^2, so the rate is 10%.

@ Averages | B
What is the average of 10, 20, 30 and 40?
= 25
- 20
- 30
- 100
? The sum is 100 and there are 4 numbers, so the average is 25.

@ Averages | I
The average of 6 numbers is 15. If one of them, 9, is removed, what is the average of the remaining numbers?
= 16.2
- 15
- 16
- 14.5
? Total = 90. Remaining total = 81 over 5 numbers, so the average is 16.2.

@ Averages | I
The average age of 5 people is 24. A sixth person aged 36 joins them. What is the new average age?
= 26
- 25
- 27
- 30
? Total age = 120 + 36 = 156, and 156 / 6 = 26.

@ Averages | A
What is the average of the first 10 natural numbers?
= 5.5
- 5
- 6
- 55
? The sum of 1 to 10 is 55, and 55 / 10 = 5.5.

@ Number System | B
Which of the following is a prime number?
= 29
- 21
- 27
- 51
? 29 has no divisors other than 1 and itself. 21 = 3 x 7, 27 = 3 x 9 and 51 = 3 x 17.

@ Number System | I
What is the LCM of 12 and 18?
= 36
- 6
- 72
- 216
? 12 = 2^2 x 3 and 18 = 2 x 3^2, so the LCM is 2^2 x 3^2 = 36.

@ Number System | I
What is the HCF of 24 and 36?
= 12
- 6
- 72
- 4
? 24 = 2^3 x 3 and 36 = 2^2 x 3^2, so the HCF is 2^2 x 3 = 12.

@ Number System | A
What is the remainder when 2^10 is divided by 7?
= 2
- 1
- 4
- 3
? 2^3 = 8 leaves remainder 1, so 2^9 leaves 1 and 2^10 leaves 2.

@ Number System | I
What is the sum of the first 20 natural numbers?
= 210
- 200
- 220
- 190
? n(n + 1) / 2 = 20 x 21 / 2 = 210.

@ Number System | A
What is the unit digit of 7^45?
= 7
- 1
- 3
- 9
? The unit digits of powers of 7 repeat every 4: 7, 9, 3, 1. Since 45 leaves remainder 1 when divided by 4, the digit is 7.

@ Permutation and Probability | B
What is the value of 5!?
= 120
- 24
- 60
- 25
? 5! = 5 x 4 x 3 x 2 x 1 = 120.

@ Permutation and Probability | I
In how many distinct ways can the letters of the word LEVEL be arranged?
= 30
- 120
- 60
- 24
? There are 5 letters with L repeated twice and E repeated twice: 5! / (2! x 2!) = 30.

@ Permutation and Probability | I
In how many ways can 2 people be chosen from a group of 6?
= 15
- 12
- 30
- 36
? 6C2 = 6 x 5 / 2 = 15.

@ Permutation and Probability | I
What is the probability of drawing a red card from a standard deck of 52 cards?
= 1/2
- 1/4
- 1/13
- 1/26
? There are 26 red cards among 52, so the probability is 1/2.

@ Permutation and Probability | A
A bag has 3 red and 5 blue balls. Two balls are drawn without replacement. What is the probability that both are red?
= 3/28
- 9/64
- 3/8
- 1/4
? P = (3/8) x (2/7) = 6/56 = 3/28.

@ Permutation and Probability | A
How many 3-digit numbers can be formed using the digits 1 to 5 without repeating any digit?
= 60
- 125
- 20
- 10
? 5 x 4 x 3 = 60.

@ Geometry and Arithmetic | B
What is the area of a rectangle that is 12 cm long and 7 cm wide?
= 84 square cm
- 38 square cm
- 19 square cm
- 96 square cm
? Area = length x width = 12 x 7 = 84.

@ Geometry and Arithmetic | I
What is the circumference of a circle of radius 7 cm? (Use 22/7 for pi.)
= 44 cm
- 22 cm
- 154 cm
- 88 cm
? Circumference = 2 x (22/7) x 7 = 44 cm.

@ Geometry and Arithmetic | I
What is the area of a triangle with base 10 cm and height 6 cm?
= 30 square cm
- 60 square cm
- 16 square cm
- 36 square cm
? Area = 1/2 x base x height = 0.5 x 10 x 6 = 30.

@ Geometry and Arithmetic | I
What is the value of (15 + 5) x 3 - 10 / 2?
= 55
- 25
- 60
- 30
? Brackets first: 20 x 3 = 60. Then 10 / 2 = 5, and 60 - 5 = 55.
